> Accessing the Settings Menu

the Dank Material Shell Settings is where you configure most of your basic things.

there is a custom bind for this: *SUPER+S*

you can also access it from multiple places in the top bar, the app launcher (*SUPER+SPACE*) and the control center (*SUPER+ESCAPE*)

the settings menu is divided into the following sections:

personalization - theming, typography, animations, sounds, time, weather and wallpapers
dank bar - basic bar settings, widgets and presets
workspaces and widgets - complex configurations for desktop widgets and bar items
dock and launcher - app launcher and toggleable dock configuration
keyboard shortcuts - graphical menu to add your own keybinds (saved to dms/binds.conf)
displays - graphical display configuration (resolution, refresh rate, layout)
network - wifi, ethernet and VPN management
system - audio, clipboard manager and multiplexer/tiling settings
power and security - lock screen and power/sleep settings
plugins - install DMS plugins to extend functionality

take the time to browse through these and try some stuff.
